/* writes docs/ASSUMED-VALUES.md from tools/assumed-data.js (every number that is NOT on the drawings).  usage: node tools/list-assumed.js */
const D=require('./assumed-data.js'),fs=require('fs'),path=require('path');
const f=v=>v==null?'—':String(v);
let o=`# ASSUMED-VALUES — every number the simulator uses that is NOT written on the ABC drawings

**Generated by \`node tools/list-assumed.js\` from \`tools/assumed-data.js\` — do not edit by hand.** Change the number in \`tools/assumed-data.js\`, run the patch and this script.
The same list is inside the app: button **Assumed values** in the Analog bar, and in the panel of each block (flagged "ASSUMED DEFAULT" / "From the Compensation file").

How to read the status column:
- **FILE** = real plant data from a file the user sent (see docs/DATA-FILES.md). Safe.
- **ASSUMED** = chosen by the assistant on the user's instruction (2026-10-07: "ikaw na ang magset … realistic default … 150 MW CFB with reheat"). NOT the DCS value. Replace with the DCS database value when it is known; typing a value in the block panel replaces the default and is saved with the project.

## 1. TP temperature compensation (${D.TP.length} blocks) — FILE
Source: \`LMYP-1 #1-Compensation Calculation of Flow.xls\`, sheet COMPENSATION (units kg/cm2g; ATM 1.03326; absolute temperature 273.15). Only **temperature** compensation exists in the file (all pressure columns are 0). The simulator uses  **DP' = DP / Kt , Kt = (T + 273.15) / (T operating + 273.15)**. The file's own coefficients agree: Kt = at · (T / span) + bt with at = span / (Top + 273.15), bt = 273.15 / (Top + 273.15) (checked for all 8 rows, \`tools/test-blocks.js\`).

| Sheet | Flow tag | Description | Temperature tag(s) | T range °C | T operating °C | at | bt |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
${D.TP.map(e=>`| ${e.sheet} | ${e.ft} (${e.kp}) | ${e.desc} | ${e.tt} | ${e.tbs} ~ ${e.tfs} | **${e.top}** | ${e.at.toFixed(6)} | ${e.bt.toFixed(6)} |`).join('\n')}

## 2. RATE ramp boxes with no number on the drawing (${D.RATE.length} boxes) — ASSUMED
The box is the ramp between the two T switches of an AUTO-MV transfer (bumpless transfer): the output follows its input at most this fast. The number is used as written (units of the signal per second). ABC-052 boxes are ignored by the user's decision; the 4 limiters of ABC-003E take their limits from inputs, they need no number.

| Sheet | Loop | Rate | Unit | Why this number |
|---|---|---|---|---|
${D.RATE.map(e=>`| ${e.sheet} | ${e.loop} | **${e.rate}** | ${e.u} | ${e.basis} |`).join('\n')}

## 3. PO / PIDV pulse output (3 PO blocks) — ASSUMED
| Pulse cycle | Full stroke time | Shortest pulse | Why |
|---|---|---|---|
| **${D.PO.cyc} s** | **${D.PO.stroke} s** | **${D.PO.minp} s** | ${D.PO.basis} |

Behaviour: every cycle the PO compares the demand with its own position (full stroke = 100 % in the stroke time); if the difference needs at least the shortest pulse it gives a raise (PO1) or lower (PO2) pulse of that length (at most one cycle) and stops when the position reaches the demand. The analog value after the PO is passed on unchanged.

## 4. ALM alarm limits (${D.ALM.length} alarms) — ASSUMED
Unit = the unit of the transmitter range written on the drawing. Empty (—) = not used. "L / LL" of pressures that are normal near zero when the unit is off (first-stage pressure, reheat pressure) are deliberately low; they will show LOW / LOW-LOW at standstill, as a real alarm would.

| Tag | HH | H | L | LL | Unit | Description | Why |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
${D.ALM.map(e=>`| ${e.tag} | ${f(e.hh)} | ${f(e.h)} | ${f(e.l)} | ${f(e.ll)} | ${e.u} | ${e.desc} | ${e.basis} |`).join('\n')}
`;
fs.writeFileSync(path.join(__dirname,'..','docs','ASSUMED-VALUES.md'),o);console.log('docs/ASSUMED-VALUES.md written',o.length,'bytes;',D.TP.length,'TP,',D.RATE.length,'RATE,',D.ALM.length,'ALM')
